invariant: INV-14
file: handshake_post.h
catches: unit_ca
reason: hspost_present_ticket leaves the pins in the session copy beside
  the ticket's PSK, so a raw or ca configuration that keeps its pins, as
  cfg.h tells a caller to, carries two auth modes and every client entry
  refuses it. A caller would then have to clear its pins to resume. The
  CA unit test presents a ticket beside its pin and requires the
  handshake to reach the socket.

--- old
#ifndef CH_TRUST_WEBPKI
    cfg->server_pubkey = NULL;
    cfg->server_pubkey_len = 0;
    cfg->server_pubkey2 = NULL;
    cfg->server_pubkey2_len = 0;
#endif
--- new
#ifndef CH_TRUST_WEBPKI
#endif
